  "description": "Adds a WebGPU render view to your app: put a WebGpuRenderView in a page, handle its Render event (or give it an IWebGpuRenderer), and record WebGPU commands into the frame it hands you. It works on every Skia head, owns its GPU device, and can run continuously at a target frame rate, render only when invalidated, or be driven frame by frame from any thread you choose. A SkiaSharp overlay draws HUD text and shapes over each frame, and the view shares its device and texture with other WebGPU libraries and with native (Rust, C, C++) modules through the CodeBrix.WebGpu hand-off contracts.",
  "iconFile": "icon-codebrix-128.png",
